{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    /* Bundler mode */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    // R18-O3: `pnpm gate` runs three tsc programs back to back and `pnpm build`
    // runs one of them again; each cold pass costs ~29-48 s on this tree. The
    // incremental cache (tsconfig.tsbuildinfo, git-ignored) turns every warm
    // pass into ~1 s with identical diagnostics — the file is pure finger-
    // printing, and TS validates it against the config and inputs.
    "incremental": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    /* Linting */
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true

    /*
      Two more strictness flags were measured on this tree. One is now ON, one is
      deliberately still OFF; both sets of numbers are `pnpm exec tsc` error counts
      with the flag added to the block above; nothing here is an estimate.

      "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true  -> ON since r19-o2 (2026-10-18).
        Measured trajectory on this tree: 85 errors with the flag flipped on
        (ede7891), 62 after the store cluster was fixed (8ffffc5), 0 after the
        lib + shell clusters (9eac0c5). r19-o2-4 flipped the same flag in
        tsconfig.tests.json and tsconfig.node.json, so all three compiler
        programs now hold the same bar. The old "31 errors" note measured an
        earlier state of the tree and is superseded.
        Every fix used an explicit guard / `??` fallback / early return — no `!`,
        no `as` (check-invariants.mjs keeps ESCAPE_HATCH_BASELINE = {}).

      "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true -> still OFF. 35 errors across 11 files
        (src/store/customize.ts 8, dialogs/ProjectSettingsDialog.tsx 8,
        components/SettingsRows.tsx 4, views/FrequentView.tsx 3, store/ui.ts 3,
        store/downloads.ts 2, views/ProjectsView.tsx 2, and 3 singletons).
        Rejecting this one is not laziness: `setRepo(slug, { alias: undefined })`
        is how the code CLEARS a field — the spread over the old value with an
        explicit undefined is the intent. exactOptionalPropertyTypes declares
        that illegal, so enabling it means redesigning the clear-semantics of
        three stores plus every prop table that passes `x ?? undefined` down.
        That is a real refactor, not a type annotation, and it belongs to the
        agents who own those components.

      Neither flag is disabled with an `any` or an `@ts-ignore` anywhere.
    */
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
